        "title": "Microcanonical Ensemble",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The microcanonical ensemble is the foundational ensemble: an isolated system with fixed energy\nE, volume V, and particle number N. No energy or particles are exchanged with any reservoir.\nThe fundamental postulate says all accessible microstates are equally probable. Entropy S = k ln Ω\nthen follows immediately. The second law becomes a counting theorem: systems evolve toward\nmacrostates with the most microstates, because those are overwhelmingly more probable."
